Well, I finally ascended a tourist.  It feels like quite an accomplishment, 
considering how when I first started playing however many years ago, I always 
thought ascended a tourist was impossible, something I'd never do.

Tourists are indeed a pain to start, considering their lack of weapons, 
armor, decent stats, etc. in the beginning.  However, they do have one thing 
going for them: time.  Their massive amount of food gives you all the time 
you need to build up your pet, sac at altars, push boulders, etc.  Plus they 
may not start with a weapon, but their weapon proficiencies allow them to use 
anything they find.

So this guy started out slow, like most tourists.  But things turned around 
once I found an altar.  Saccing gave me Mjollnir, so that turned things 
around.  But I didn't find much in the way of other equipment.  After getting 
Mjollnir, I went down to Sokoban, and finished that.  Was surprised to find, 
while playing offline, that I've memorized all the solutions to Sokoban.  
After Sokoban, it was time for the mines.  Went down to minetown, no 
coaligned altar, but my pet cat, which was now an ice devil thanks to a wand 
of poly, killed the priest.  Dove down a few more levels, to find a luckstone 
on a random dwarf.  Decided I didn't need to risk going down to the bottom, 
despite there often being good items down there.  No wishes in minetown 
either, so my equipment was still pretty bad.  Found a bones level from 
hearse with SDSM, and despite the fact I would've preferred grey, I decided 
it was still good.  While waiting to start the Quest, I did Ludios.  Found 
some grey dragon scales there, and made me GDSM.  Had an amulet of 
reflection, too, so was able to protect myself a lot more.  Despite numerous 
soldiers, didn't find a silver saber.  Got my protection filled out, and did 
the quest.  Found some boots of speed along the way.  With the quest done, 
down to the castle, filled out my equipment, and went down to Gehennom.

Gehennom was...boring as usual.  Knew magic mapping, so saved myself a little 
time.  Made my final preperations, and stormed Rodney's tower.  Soon I was to 
the elemental planes.

Ran into quite a bit of trouble on fire, when Archons surrounded me with 
summoned monsters.  Rodney double-troubled me and then stole the amulet, 
which I thought was the end for this char.  But after posting to this ng and 
receiving some great advice (thanks everyone), I remembered I had a ring of 
conflict, and that solved the problem nicely.  Was able to get to water, and 
then astral in short order.

Noticed once I got to Astral that my PYEC was gone, apparantly stolen by 
Rodney on water.  Oops.  First went left, with Death, but that was Chaotic.  
Then center, with Famine, and that was Lawful.  On the way right, with 
Pestilence, I managed to go down to 0 hp and die, but fortunately I had my 
amulet of life-saving on.  Was kinda foolish...if I had been paying closer 
attention to my hp, the death could've been avoided.  Oh well.  Plowed my way 
through, blew my magic whistle, and offered.

So I'm down to three classes left to ascend: Ranger, Healer, and Monk.  I 
think I'll try to ascend a neutral Ranger first, since I have no idea what 
weapon a chaotic one would use.  I guess they'd have to get their weapon 
through saccing.  Personally, I normally hate saccing for a weapon, since you 
tend to get so much junk.  I prefer to see if I can use a magic lamp wish for 
something better, before I see any other artifacts.  Anyway, Ranger shouldn't 
be *too* bad, and Monks are doable (had a nice monk that died on plane of 
fire awhile ago...real shame, he'd managed to keep his vegetarian conduct 
that far), but Healer is just gonna be a pain.  Oh well, no one said 
ascending every class was gonna be easy.

